style=3D'mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style=3D'font-family:"Calibri",=
sans-serif'>
of the story:</span></b><span style=3D'font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif'><o=
:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span style=3D'font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif'>Zion =
soldiers
Ricochet, Sun Bear, Breaker, Zeus, and Boatman are patrolling for gifted hu=
mans
to pull out of the matrix power plant #DDZ8TA Alpha. They find a target wor=
th
investigating at a cyber caf&eacute; called &#8220;Mirrors&#8221;.<o:p></o:=
p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span style=3D'font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif'><o:p>=
&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span style=3D'font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif'>Part =
1 -<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span style=3D'font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif'>The g=
roup
receives a beacon that indicates they have a phone message in the Matrix. T=
he
group is loaded into the Matrix in a safe house they secured last time they
visited the <span class=3DGramE>Matrix,</span> they need to go inside <span
class=3DGramE>in order to</span> check the phone message. The message was f=
or an
alias the group created called &#8220;the Jackal&#8221;. The caller is
confused, as most &#8220;reds&#8221; are when they call. The caller identif=
ies
himself as Billy. Billy <span class=3DGramE>ask</span> if they got the lett=
er he
sent on the message. They didn&#8217;t get a beacon about the letter, but t=
he
caller <span class=3DGramE>leaves</span> the PO Box he sent the mail too. B=
ut
they should have gotten a signal beacon of some sort. (Operator would be the
beacon. The PO Box is one that he monitors. It might have been trapped by t=
he
AI. They might have changed the code to hide the letter.) It is easy for the
group to check out the parcel in the PO Box and get the target <span
class=3DSpellE><span class=3DGramE>redpill&#8217;s</span></span> address. (=
The
parcel is bugged with a beacon trap. The beacon program goes off once the m=
ail
is touched, or disturbed. The parcel can tell if a non <span class=3DSpellE=
>bluepill</span>
touches it.) The group needs to get a location for the target (&#8220;Billy=
&#8221;)
who is calling. The target is a teenager named &#8220;Billy Bobbin&#8221;. =
He
wants to meet <span class=3DGramE>the Jackal</span> because he is looking f=
or
answers. Billy is legit. He goes to high school in Denver. He is a B student
that keeps his nose clean. Until recently he did everything he was told.<o:=
p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span style=3D'font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif'><o:p>=
&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span style=3D'font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif'>Duh <=
span
class=3DSpellE>duh</span> <span class=3DSpellE>duh</span>! Drama begins. Wh=
y is
there an agent leaving the PO Box. The Post Office is a great place for an
Agent <span class=3DGramE>encounter, but</span> avoid encountering an Agent=
 if
the Threat counter for this session is low. The Agents are <span class=3DGr=
amE>on
to</span> this <span class=3DGramE>Billy</span> and they are looking for si=
milar
clues. The team gets Billy&#8217;s <span class=3DGramE>information</span> b=
ut
they can&#8217;t find him at home or in his normal places. Before the team
encounters Billy at home or in his usual <span class=3DGramE>haunts</span> =
he
disappears. <s><o:p></o:p></s></span></p>

